Adding the Final Touches
In the following steps, you will add a scripted component to the project you have been working on
during this hour to make it all work:
1. Create a new folder called Scripts and add a new script to it. Name the script
AnimationControl. Attach the script to the Ethan model in the scene. (This step is important!)
2. Add the following code to the AnimationControl script:
Animator anim;
void Start ()
{
// Get a reference to the animator
anim = GetComponent<Animator> ();
}
void Update ()
{
anim.SetFloat ("Speed", Input.GetAxis ("Vertical"));
anim.SetFloat ("Direction", Input.GetAxis("Horizontal"));
}
3. Run the scene and notice that the animations are controlled with the vertical and horizontal
input axes. (Recall that the horizontal and vertical input axes are mapped to the WASD keys
and the arrow keys.)
