Audio Scripting 385
As the name implies, this variable is true if the audio is currently playing and false if it is not.
Starting and Stopping Audio
This exercise shows you how to use scripts to start and stop an audio clip. It uses the scene cre-
ated in the Try It Yourself “Adding Audio in the Scene View.” If you have not completed that scene
yet, do so before continuing. Follow these steps:
1. Open the scene you created in the Try It Yourself “Adding Audio in the Scene View.”
2. On the Cube game object created previously, locate the Audio Source component. Uncheck
the Play On Wake property and check the Loop property.
3. Create a new folder named Scripts and create a new script in it called AudioScript. Attach
the script to the cube. Change the script’s code to the following:
using UnityEngine;
public class AudioScript : MonoBehaviour
{
AudioSource audioSource;
void Start()
{
audioSource = GetComponent<AudioSource>();
}
void Update()
{
if (Input.GetButtonDown("Jump"))
{
if (audioSource.isPlaying == true)
audioSource.Stop();
else
audioSource.Play();
}
}
}
